.TH GSEXPLORER-PLUS 1 "October 2026" "GSExplorer+ 26.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gsexplorer-plus \- dual-pane file manager (GSExplorer+)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gsexplorer-plus
[\fIFOLDER\fR | \fIFILE\fR | \fIfile:///URI\fR]
.br
.B gsexplorer-plus
\-\-sync \fIPROFILE\fR [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-quiet]
.br
.B gsexplorer-plus
\-\-list\-profiles
.br
.B gsexplorer-plus
\-\-version | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
GSExplorer+ is a keyboard-friendly, dual-pane file manager with tabs, a
breadcrumb path bar, a background file-operation queue, freedesktop.org trash
support and themes. When FOLDER is given it opens in a new tab in the left
pane; when FILE is given its folder opens with the file selected.
.SH SYNC AND BACKUP
Tools > Sync & Backup (Ctrl+Shift+B) manages profiles of folder-pair tasks; Ctrl+Shift+S
compares the two pane folders. Modes: \fBMirror\fR (target becomes an exact copy),
\fBUpdate\fR (copy new/newer, never delete), \fBTwo-way\fR (propagate changes and deletions
both ways; conflicts are shown for you to resolve) and \fBSnapshot backup\fR (dated copies;
unchanged files are hard links to the previous snapshot). Overwritten and deleted files go
to the trash, a versions folder, or are deleted, per task.
While Synchronize runs, a progress window shows the percentage done with a turning gear and
a countdown of the estimated time left, the direction data is moving (left to right, right to
left, deleting on one side, or into a new snapshot), the operation in progress with its full
source and destination paths, a bar for the current file, and files, data, speed, elapsed and
remaining time. Pause, Cancel (files already copied stay; nothing is left half-written) and
Run in background are available; "Show progress" in the Sync window brings it back.
.TP
.B \-\-sync \fIPROFILE\fR
Run a saved profile without a GUI (used by scheduled runs). Conflicts are skipped.
Prints a JSON summary. Exit status: 0 success, 1 warnings, 2 errors, 3 cancelled.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
With \-\-sync: show what would happen; change nothing.
.SH CONNECT
Connect > Connect to Server (Ctrl+K) mounts SMB, SFTP, FTP/FTPS, WebDAV and NFS shares through
GVFS (they open as normal folders), opens SSH sessions in your terminal, and starts Remmina or
FreeRDP for RDP/VNC. OneDrive and Google Drive work through GNOME Online Accounts or rclone.
Passwords are passed to the mount helper on standard input and, if you choose, stored only in
the system keyring (libsecret). Unknown SSH host keys must be confirmed; changed keys are refused.
.SH PREVIEW
Alt+P toggles the preview panel: images, text, PDF first page, DOCX/PPTX/XLSX/ODF text,
video and audio playback (or hand-off to VLC). Icon view shows thumbnails from the shared
freedesktop cache; external thumbnailers run sandboxed with bubblewrap when available.
.SH PLAYER
Double-clicking a video or audio file opens GSExplorer+ Player (Preferences can choose the system
app or VLC instead). It plays the folder as a playlist, with fullscreen, speed 0.5x to 2x, audio and
subtitle tracks, cover art, repeat/shuffle, and resumes long files where you stopped (positions are
kept in ~/.local/share/gsexplorer-plus/media-positions.json). Keys: Space play/pause, Left/Right 5 s,
J/L 10 s, Up/Down volume, M mute, F fullscreen, N/P next/previous, [ ] speed.
.SH FIND FILES
The magnifying-glass toolbar button, Ctrl+F or Alt+F7 (or right-click a folder > Search in…) opens
Find Files. Search by name (contains, wildcards such as *.pdf;*.docx, regular expression or exact),
text inside files (plain or regular expression, whole word, NOT containing; also inside DOCX, XLSX,
PPTX and ODF documents, and PDFs when pdftotext from poppler-utils is installed), files or folders,
kind, size, modification date, empty items and names inside .zip/.tar archives, with depth limit,
hidden files, folders to skip and stay-on-this-drive options. With plocate installed, name searches
can use the system file index. Results appear while searching and can be sorted, filtered, refined,
previewed (matching line highlighted), opened, viewed (F3), shown in GSExplorer+, copied, moved,
compressed, trashed or exported to CSV. Searches can be saved by name.
.SH ARCHIVES
Right-click selected items > \fBCompress…\fR (Alt+F5) creates .zip, .tar.gz, .tar.xz, .tar.bz2 or .tar
(built in), .tar.zst (needs zstd) or .7z with an optional password (needs 7zip). On an archive,
\fBExtract here\fR, \fBExtract to "name/"\fR and \fBExtract to…\fR (Alt+F9) unpack it; .7z, .rar and
.iso need 7zip. Extraction goes through a hidden staging folder, never overwrites existing files, refuses
absolute and ".." paths and links leading outside the folder, drops setuid bits, and stops before the
disk fills up.
.SH TERMINAL
F12 or "Open terminal here" opens your terminal in the folder shown in the active pane; right-clicking
a folder offers "Open terminal in <folder>". The folder is passed with the terminal's own option
(e.g. --working-directory), as the starting folder and as $PWD. A custom terminal command in
Preferences may contain {dir} for the folder.
.SH FIND DUPLICATES
Tools > Find Duplicates (Ctrl+Shift+D), or "Find duplicates in this folder" on a folder's context menu,
searches one or more folders. \fBIdentical content\fR groups files by size, then a hash of the first and
last 16 KiB, then a full BLAKE2b-256 hash, so only same-size candidates are read in full. \fBSame name
and size\fR and \fBSame name only\fR do not compare contents. Hard links are listed once (removing one
frees no space). Symlinks, pipes and devices are never read; /proc, /sys, /dev and /run are skipped.
Results are grouped and sortable by wasted space, size, copies, name, location or date; selecting a copy
previews it next to another copy of the same group. Selected copies can be moved to the trash, deleted, or
moved into an audit folder (GSExplorer-duplicates-DATE) that keeps each file's full original path and a
manifest.csv (original path, new path, hash, kept copy); "Undo an audit move" restores from it. Every
action re-checks size and modification time against the scan and always leaves one copy per group.
.SH KEYS
F2 rename, F3 view (Left/Right or the arrow buttons step through the folder's files), F4 edit, F5 copy, F6 move, F7 new folder, F8/Delete trash,
Shift+Delete delete permanently, Tab switch pane, F9 toggle dual pane,
Ctrl+S quick filter, Ctrl+H hidden files, Ctrl+J operations queue.
Help > Keyboard shortcuts lists all keys.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gsexplorer-plus/config.json
Settings, bookmarks and the last session.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gsexplorer-plus/themes/*.json
User themes. Files override built-in themes with the same name.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gsexplorer-plus/sync/*.json
Sync & Backup profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/gsexplorer-plus/sync-logs/
Run logs (last 100 kept). Two-way state databases live in ../sync-state/.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/gsexplorer-plus-sync-*.timer
Schedules created by the Schedule dialog (systemd user timers).
.TP
.I ~/.config/gsexplorer-plus/connections.json
Saved connections (mode 0600; never contains passwords).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails/
Shared freedesktop thumbnail cache.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Trash
Home trash (freedesktop.org Trash specification).
.SH PRIVACY
No telemetry and no auto-update. GSExplorer+ only uses the network when you connect to a server or
open a network location.
.SH EXIT STATUS
For \-\-sync: 0 success, 1 warnings, 2 errors, 3 cancelled.
.SH MIGRATION
Version 26.8.0 renamed GExplorer to GSExplorer+. On first start, settings and data in
~/.config/gexplorer, ~/.local/share/gexplorer and ~/.cache/gexplorer move to the
gsexplorer-plus folders (only when the new folders do not exist yet), and scheduled
gexplorer-sync-* timers are re-created as gsexplorer-plus-sync-*. The old unit files are kept
with a .migrated suffix. Passwords saved in the keyring under the old name keep working.
The \fBgexplorer\fR command remains as an alias for one transition period.
